  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset landscape in late 2026 is characterized by a dual focus on the maturation of Bitcoin as institutional infrastructure and the growing influence of deterministic smart contract models, particularly on Bitcoin. Spot Bitcoin ETFs have solidified their role, managing over $100B in assets and establishing Bitcoin as a core portfolio component. Concurrently, regulatory headwinds in the U.S., exemplified by continued legislative friction around the CLARITY Act, are driving developers towards more predictable, non-Turing complete smart contract solutions like Clarity. This shift is occurring alongside advancements in native cross-chain interoperability, enabling direct liquidity flow from Bitcoin to EVM ecosystems without relying on centralized wrapped assets. Ethereum continues to be the dominant settlement and execution layer for DeFi, maintaining its 'Peak Hype' status.",
